These and other factors, many of which are beyond our control, may cause our operating results and the market price and demand for our shares to fluctuate substantially. While we believe that operating results for any particular quarter are not necessarily a meaningful indication of future results, fluctuations in our quarterly operating results could limit or prevent investors from readily selling their shares and may otherwise negatively affect the market price and liquidity of our shares. In addition, in the past, a securities class action litigation has been brought against the Company in connection with the volatility of our stock price. If any of our stockholders brought a similar

lawsuit against us in the future, we could incur substantial costs defending and/or settling the lawsuit. Such a lawsuit could also divert the time and attention of our management from our business, which could significantly harm our profitability and reputation.

The following types of expenses are included in our selling, general, and administrative costs (“SG&A”):

payroll and benefit costs of pet care center employees and corporate employees;

occupancy and operating costs of pet care centers and corporate facilities;

